expect: written
note: written
keeps: before
bars: \bno longer counts\b | \bremoverejected\b
why: Kirill found a note that said a section "no longer counts" once its entries are gone hard to follow; the fact is told as the steps a reader can watch, where the currency sits only on the entries and removing them all leaves nothing that marks the section, and the order of removal follows from those steps
labelled: 2026-09-30
--- code
export function removeRejected(book: Book, rejected: Set<string>): void {
  book.sections.filter((section) => rejected.has(section.id)).forEach((section) => book.removeSection(section));
  book.entries.filter((entry) => rejected.has(entry.id)).forEach((entry) => book.removeEntry(entry));
}
--- facts
A ledger section may state its currency only on its entries.
Once every entry of a section is removed, nothing marks the section as settled in that currency, so a rejected section is found only while its entries remain.
